# Derived by hand from Semantics ch. 7 (a `rebuild` builds a new generation after each tick its source moves, the old one torn down): the zoom moves the inner `rebuild`'s source at 1, under the page's standing generation.
test the_inner_rebuild_follows_the_block

tick 0
  added:
    0: Ui.Button(label="next")
    1: Ui.Button(label="zoom")
    2/#0/0: Ui.Label(text="page 1")
    2/#0/1/#0/0: Ui.Label(text="zoom 1")

tick 1
  in:
    1: click
  added:
    2/#0/1/#1/0: Ui.Label(text="zoom 2")
  torn down:
    2/#0/1/#0/0: Ui.Label(text="zoom 1")
